<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reconquista</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Reconquista refers to the centuries-long series of campaigns by Christian kingdoms of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a> to conquer the territories ruled by Muslims, completed with the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> in 1492. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a> intervened in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> to resist it. Its completion and crusading ethos shaped the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reconquista.jpg" alt="Reconquista" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Creator:Abdula · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cantigas_battle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
